MT-InfoSeek licensing
=====================

The MT-InfoSeek release combines original code, dataset records, and material
derived from several upstream sources. License terms differ by component;
licenses are inherited from the upstream where applicable.

Original code in this repository
--------------------------------

Original code written for MT-InfoSeek (the data-generation pipelines,
evaluators, scripts, and Croissant builder) is released under Apache License
2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

Dataset records
---------------

Released dataset files (under `data/`) are licensed CC-BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), inherited from their upstream
sources where applicable.

Per-component upstream provenance
---------------------------------

Logic-Q-MT (`data/logic_q_mt.csv`)
    Derived from QuestBench Logic-Q
    (https://github.com/google-deepmind/questbench), CC-BY 4.0.

GSME-Q-MT (`data/gsme_q_mt.csv`)
    Derived from QuestBench GSM-Q
    (https://github.com/google-deepmind/questbench), CC-BY 4.0.

GSME-Q-MT-Ext (`data/gsme_q_mt_ext.csv`)
    Same generator as GSME-Q-MT, extended with rule-graph metadata, distractor
    variables, alternative-path detection, and forbid-alternatives query sets.
    Derived from QuestBench GSM-Q, CC-BY 4.0.

GeneReg-MT (`data/genereg_mt.jsonl`)
    Built on Boolean gene-regulatory network models from
    Kadelka et al. (2024), https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-024-03900-1.
    Open access via the original publication; no specific license declared
    upstream. The MT-InfoSeek-generated task instances are released CC-BY 4.0.

20 Questions concept lists (`data/data_20q.py`)
    Adapted from the UoT 20-Questions release
    (https://github.com/lzy-xmu/UoT) and the BIG-bench 20-Questions concept
    set. No explicit license was identified in the upstream release; users
    should consult the upstream source terms.

Third-party code provenance
---------------------------

Portions of the Logic-Q and GSME-Q data-generation and evaluator scaffold are
derived from https://github.com/google-deepmind/questbench and are licensed
under Apache License 2.0. Logic-Q files that retain upstream copyright headers
preserve those notices in place.
